       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity. It may be a typo for 100 mg.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose.\n- **Another dose of 200 mg/day or less.** Tell me the dose.\n\nIf 1000 mg is intended, for example under a specific protocol, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending before it's entered.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
